## What is Downward API?
Exposes Pod/container metadata (name, namespace, labels, annotations, node info, resource requests/limits) to containers **without calling API server**.

## 2 Ways to Expose:

| Method | Use Case |
|--------|----------|
| **Environment Variables** | Simple values (Pod name, namespace, node, IP, service account) |
| **DownwardAPI Volume (File)** | Labels & annotations (all as files) |

---

## Available Fields

### Via `fieldRef` (Env + Volume)
- `metadata.name` – Pod name
- `metadata.namespace` – Pod namespace
- `metadata.uid` – Pod UID
- `metadata.labels['<KEY>']` – Specific label value
- `metadata.annotations['<KEY>']` – Specific annotation value

### Via `fieldRef` (Env ONLY – Not Volume)
- `spec.serviceAccountName` – Service account name
- `spec.nodeName` – Node name
- `status.hostIP` – Node IP
- `status.podIP` – Pod IP

### Via DownwardAPI Volume (File ONLY – Not Env)
- `metadata.labels` – All labels (label-key="value")
- `metadata.annotations` – All annotations (annotation-key="value")

### Via `resourceFieldRef` (Env + Volume)
- `limits.cpu` / `requests.cpu`
- `limits.memory` / `requests.memory`
- `limits.ephemeral-storage` / `requests.ephemeral-storage`
- `limits.hugepages-*` / `requests.hugepages-*`


