check env var given in pod
---------------------------------------------------------------------

| Method | Shows in printenv? | Realtime Command to Check |
|--------|-------------------|---------------------------|
| Direct `env` (key: value)        | ✅ Yes (shows value)         | `k exec <pod> -- printenv` |
| FieldRef `fieldRef`(metadata.name| ✅ Yes (shows value) | `k exec <pod> -- printenv \| grep POD_NAME` |
| ConfigMap → `env` (individual)   | ✅ Yes (shows value)         | `k exec <pod> -- printenv \| grep <KEY>` |
| ConfigMap → `envFrom` (all keys) | ✅ Yes (shows all key=value) | `k exec <pod> -- env` |
| ConfigMap → Volume Mount         | ❌ No (file, not env)        | `k exec <pod> -- cat /path/to/configmap/file` |
| Secret → Volume Mount            | ❌ No (file, not env)        | `k exec <pod> -- cat /path/to/secret/file` |

| Secret → `env` (individual)      | ❌ No (value masked)         | `k get secret <name> -o jsonpath='{.data.<key>}' \| base64 -d` |  --DIFFICULT TO REMEMBER
| Secret → `envFrom` (all keys)    | ❌ No (values masked)        | `k get secret <name> -o yaml` |                                   --DIFFICULT 


